module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.FiniteTypeLocalReflector
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.SheafifiedCechIndependence
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The object of Tag 099E for a merely locally generated sheaf of ideals

[Stacks, Tag 099E] is stated for a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` of **finite type**: no family of
global sections need generate it, only finitely many sections over each member of a covering
family. This file records that in that regime the object built in `SheafifiedCech.lean` from a
family of *global* sections is available on each slice of a cover, which is where the source's
construction takes place.

Three statements then make up the local half of the tag, for an `ℐ` that is only locally
generated:

* on each slice `(𝒞/U_i, 𝒪_{U_i})` of a covering family, `ℐ|_{U_i}` *is* generated by finitely
  many global sections — `exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal` below;
* for such a family there is the complex `K ⟶ 𝒪_{U_i}` —
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafifiedCech` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafifiedCechAugmentation`, the sheafification of the presheaf of
  complexes `U' ↦ K(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))`;
* and it does not depend on the family chosen: any other finite family generating the same sheaf
  of ideals gives an isomorphic object over `𝒪`, on the slices over a covering sieve —
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_mem_sieve_iso_sheafifiedCech`.

What is *not* here is the passage from these to a single `K ⟶ 𝒪` on `𝒞` itself. The source makes
it by restricting to the full subcategory of objects over which `ℐ` is finitely generated — a
special cocontinuous functor, [Stacks, Tag 03CG] — and then gluing the `K_U^\bullet`, which is
descent for complexes of sheaves along a covering family and not an instance of the locality of
*morphisms* in `D(𝒪)`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`). Neither step is proved here,
and neither is needed: the tag is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech` of `FiniteTypeExtendedCech.lean`,
which takes another route (see the status note below). No `@[stacks 099E]` attribute is attached
in this file, because what it proves is the construction of the tag's object on the slices and
its independence of the generators, not the tag.

**Status.** [Stacks, Tag 099E] is proved for an arbitrary sheaf of ideals, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isGlobalExtendedCech` of `FiniteTypeExtendedCech.lean`,
and [Stacks, Tag 099F] follows from it as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete` of `FiniteTypeReflector.lean`.
Neither [Stacks, Tag 099D] nor any gluing is used there: the presheaf of Čech complexes of *all*
local generators of `ℐ` — a filtered colimit, hence a presheaf with no choice made — is
sheafified on `𝒞`, and on each slice the leg into it from the Čech complex of one generating
family is locally bijective on homology. Where the notes
below say that 099E is missing or needs gluing, they record the state of the library before
that construction.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal`: **a sheaf of
  ideals of finite type is generated by finitely many global sections on each slice of a covering
  family**, so that the object of `SheafifiedCech.lean` applies there.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03CG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **A sheaf of ideals of finite type is generated by finitely many global sections on each
slice of a covering family.** The finite-type condition supplies a covering family `{U_i}` and,
over each `U_i`, finitely many sections of `ℐ` generating it; those sections are global sections
of `𝒪_{U_i}` (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection`) and the sheaf of ideals they
generate on the slice is `ℐ|_{U_i}` on the nose
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_of_generates`).

This is the hypothesis under which `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafifiedCech` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafifiedCechAugmentation` give the complex `K ⟶ 𝒪` of
[Stacks, Tag 099E] on the slice, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_mem_sieve_iso_sheafifiedCech` its independence of the
chosen generators. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal
    (hI : PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType X.J I.toSheafOfModules.val) :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C), X.J.CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : ι, ∃ (n : ℕ) (gens : Fin n →
          Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over (V i)).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})),
        overIdeal I (V i) = idealOfGlobalSections (X.over (V i)) gens := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, hgen⟩ := hI.exists_generators
  refine ⟨ι, V, hV, fun i => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨n, sect, hs⟩ := hgen i
  exact ⟨n, fun j => globalSectionOfSection X (V i) (sect j).val,
    overIdeal_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_of_generates X (V i) I sect hs⟩

/-- **The same, at Mathlib's finite-type condition** — the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 099E] —
turned into the sectionwise one by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteType`. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_of_isFiniteType
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C), X.J.CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : ι, ∃ (n : ℕ) (gens : Fin n →
          Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over (V i)).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})),
        overIdeal I (V i) = idealOfGlobalSections (X.over (V i)) gens :=
  exists_coversTop_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal X I
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteType I.toSheafOfModules inferInstance)

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
